   "he": "מֵהֵיכָן קוֹרֵא אָדָם אֶת הַמְּגִילָּה וְכוּ׳. תַּנְיָא, רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן יוֹחַאי אוֹמֵר: מִ״בַּלַּיְלָה הַהוּא״.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that three Sages disagree about the question: Beginning «from where must a person read the Megilla» in order to fulfill his obligation? «It is taught» in a baraita that there is a fourth opinion as well: «Rabbi Shimon bar Yoḥai says:» One must start to read from «“On that night”» (Esther 6:1)."
  }
